From: Shaan Majid <70789625+shaanmajid@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ca-certificates: blacklist emSign ECC Root CA - G3

The private keys of eight eMudhra intermediate CAs have been
compromised. Their TLS issuer, emSign Root TLS CA - G3, is cross-signed
by emSign ECC Root CA - G3. NSS 3.131.1 removes that root (Mozilla bug
2084101), but no Debian release carries the removal yet.

Blacklist the root so certdata2pem.py skips it.

Signed-off-by: Shaan Majid <70789625+shaanmajid@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/mozilla/blacklist.txt
+++ b/mozilla/blacklist.txt
@@ -4,3 +4,6 @@
 "Explicitly Distrust DigiNotar Root CA"
 
 # Expired CAs
+
+# Compromised intermediate CAs chain to this root (Mozilla bug 2084101)
+"emSign ECC Root CA - G3"
